.TH io_uring_memory_size 3 "November 11, 2026" "liburing-2.11" "liburing Manual"
.SH NAME
io_uring_memory_size \- return the memory size needed for a ring
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <liburing.h>
.PP
.BI "ssize_t io_uring_memory_size(unsigned " entries ", unsigned " flags ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The
.BR io_uring_memory_size (3)
function returns the amount of memory, in bytes, needed for the rings of an
io_uring set up with
.I entries
SQ entries and the setup flags given in
.IR flags .
This covers the SQ and CQ rings, the SQ index array, and the array of SQEs,
each rounded up to the page size.

As when setting up a ring,
.I entries
is rounded up to the next power of two, and the CQ ring is twice the size of
the SQ ring. The flags that change the layout of the rings, such as
.BR IORING_SETUP_SQE128 ,
.BR IORING_SETUP_CQE32
and
.BR IORING_SETUP_NO_SQARRAY ,
are taken into account. To specify the size of the CQ ring, use
.BR io_uring_memory_size_params (3)
instead.

This is useful for applications that provide the memory for the rings
themselves, see
.BR io_uring_queue_init_mem (3),
or that want to know the memory footprint of a ring before setting it up.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the needed memory size in bytes on success. On failure, a negative
errno value is returned:
.TP
.B -EINVAL
.I entries
is 0, or is larger than the kernel maximum and
.B IORING_SETUP_CLAMP
is not set in
.IR flags ,
or
.B IORING_SETUP_CQSIZE
is set in
.IR flags .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR io_uring_memory_size_params (3),
.BR io_uring_mlock_size (3),
.BR io_uring_queue_init (3),
.BR io_uring_queue_init_mem (3)
